<i>AVAILABLE.</i>

221
00:15:42,025 --> 00:15:44,486
Director:
<i>AND WE’RE OUT, FOLKS.</i>

222
00:15:44,527 --> 00:15:46,029
THAT’S NOT THE WAY
IT’S SUPPOSED TO BE.

223
00:15:46,071 --> 00:15:47,655
NO, WE REHEARSED
IT DIFFERENTLY.

224
00:15:49,616 --> 00:15:53,119
IT’S OKAY.
NICE WORK, BOBBY.

225
00:15:53,161 --> 00:15:55,163
HEY, LADIES, CAN YOU
EXCUSE US FOR A MINUTE?

226
00:15:57,165 --> 00:15:59,376
WHERE WAS THE BIG FINISH,
BOBBY, HMM?

227
00:15:59,417 --> 00:16:01,044
YOU TELL YOUR STORY,
YOU THANK YOUR PRETTY WIFE.

228
00:16:01,086 --> 00:16:02,379
<i>YOU BRING HER OUT</i>
<i>FOR A BIG HUG AND KISS.</i>

229
00:16:02,420 --> 00:16:04,089
I JUST DIDN’T WANT
TO PUSH IT, ALL RIGHT?

230
00:16:04,130 --> 00:16:05,799
OKAY, BUT THAT’S
THE HEART OF THE STORY.

231
00:16:05,840 --> 00:16:09,052
SHE WAS THERE
FOR YOUR WHOLE RECOVERY.

232
00:16:09,094 --> 00:16:11,471
AND WITHOUT THE ACKNOWLEDGMENT,
WITHOUT THE KISS,

233
00:16:11,513 --> 00:16:14,057
THE AUDIENCE ISN’T
GONNA HAVE ANY KIND OF
EMOTIONAL CONNECTION.

234
00:16:14,099 --> 00:16:16,351
I DISAGREE. TOO MUCH
EMOTION AND IT’S GONNA
FEEL LIKE PANDERING.

235
00:16:16,393 --> 00:16:18,478
OKAY, WHY DON’T YOU LET ME
DO THE PUBLIC RELATIONS

236
00:16:18,520 --> 00:16:20,146
AND YOU DO THE LEGAL
PAPERWORK, OKAY?

237
00:16:20,188 --> 00:16:22,691
OKAY, I GET IT, SUZANNE,
ALL RIGHT?  IT’S MY FAULT.

238
00:16:22,732 --> 00:16:25,318
IT WASN’T YOUR FAULT,
BOBBY.

239
00:16:25,360 --> 00:16:28,154
YOU WERE FINE.
JUST REMEMBER YOUR
BULLET POINTS NEXT TIME.

240
00:16:28,196 --> 00:16:30,323
- I WILL.
- THESE INTERVIEWS
ARE IMPORTANT.

241
00:16:30,365 --> 00:16:32,158
Man: <i>NINA, RELAX.</i>

242
00:16:32,200 --> 00:16:35,120
DON’T WORRY ABOUT THEM.
YOU WERE GREAT.

243
00:16:35,161 --> 00:16:38,665
- YEAH?
- YOUR STORY’S REAL
AND PEOPLE FEEL THAT.

244
00:16:38,707 --> 00:16:42,168
I KNOW THAT YOU GET
OVERWHELMED AT TIMES,

245
00:16:42,210 --> 00:16:46,172
BUT WE HAVE TO KEEP
MOVING FORWARD, BOBBY.

246
00:16:46,214 --> 00:16:47,716
YOU WERE MEANT
TO DO THIS.

247
00:16:52,220 --> 00:16:55,724
I KNOW.
I KNOW, BABY.

248
00:16:55,765 --> 00:16:57,767
- <i>BOBBY.</i>
- YEAH?

249
00:16:57,809 --> 00:16:59,811
WE GOT THE JIGSAW
SURVIVOR GROUP TOMORROW.

250
00:16:59,853 --> 00:17:01,438
30 MINUTES OF FACE TIME
WITH OTHER SURVIVORS.

251
00:17:01,479 --> 00:17:04,149
YEAH, SOUNDS GOOD.

252
00:17:04,190 --> 00:17:06,401
- NOTHING MORE
EXCITING THAN THAT.
- NO, NOT MUCH.

253
00:17:06,443 --> 00:17:07,736
LET’S GO.

254
00:17:11,239 --> 00:17:13,241
<i>( police radio chatter )</i>

255
00:17:27,672 --> 00:17:30,592
( shrieks )

256
00:17:30,633 --> 00:17:33,762
<i>( mechanical whirring )</i>

257
00:17:49,361 --> 00:17:51,446
( gasps )
OH GOD!

258
00:17:51,488 --> 00:17:54,449
YOU WANT TO KNOW
THE ONLY THING WRONG
WITH KILLING YOU, JILL?

259
00:17:55,867 --> 00:17:57,369
I CAN ONLY DO IT ONCE.

260
00:18:00,747 --> 00:18:03,750
- <i>( clicking )</i>
- ( whimpering )

261
00:18:07,504 --> 00:18:11,174
OH MY GOD!
NO!

262
00:18:19,974 --> 00:18:21,309
NO!

263
00:18:25,313 --> 00:18:27,440
( gasps )

264
00:18:45,875 --> 00:18:47,919
( grunts )

265
00:18:47,961 --> 00:18:50,505
HELP ME!
HELP ME!

266
00:18:50,547 --> 00:18:53,758
HELP!
FUCK!

267
00:18:53,800 --> 00:18:55,635
Jigsaw:
<i>Hello, Evan.</i>

268
00:18:55,677 --> 00:18:57,721
<i>I want to play a game.</i>

269
00:18:57,762 --> 00:19:01,182
<i>The situation</i>
<i>you find yourself in</i>
<i>is of your own doing.</i>

270
00:19:01,224 --> 00:19:03,852
<i>You, your girlfriend</i>
<i>and your friends</i>

271
00:19:03,893 --> 00:19:07,355
<i>are all racists.</i>

272
00:19:07,397 --> 00:19:10,191
EVAN, YOU FUCK.
YOU GET ME OUT OF HERE!

273
00:19:10,233 --> 00:19:11,860
<i>You have</i>
<i>intimidated others...</i>

274
00:19:11,901 --> 00:19:14,195
- WHAT THE FUCK?
- <i>...based on their</i>
<i>physical differences.</i>

275
00:19:14,237 --> 00:19:17,240
- <i>But today it is you</i>
<i>who will run scared.</i>
- WHAT THE FUCK, MAN?

276
00:19:17,282 --> 00:19:20,952
<i>Your pathetic friends</i>
<i>follow your every</i>
<i>word, Evan.</i>

277
00:19:20,994 --> 00:19:24,622
<i>Therefore, you will be</i>
<i>the only one capable</i>

278
00:19:24,664 --> 00:19:27,751
<i>of saving them</i>
<i>and yourself.</i>

279
00:19:30,337 --> 00:19:33,715
<i>In 30 seconds,</i>
<i>the jacks holding up</i>
<i>this car will fall...</i>

280
00:19:33,757 --> 00:19:35,800
( wailing )

281
00:19:35,842 --> 00:19:38,219
<i>...setting off</i>
<i>a deadly chain of events.</i>

282
00:19:38,261 --> 00:19:40,722
<i>In order to stop this</i>
<i>from happening,</i>

283
00:19:40,764 --> 00:19:42,891
<i>you must tear</i>
<i>yourself away</i>

284
00:19:42,932 --> 00:19:45,935
<i>from the seat</i>
<i>to which you are glued.</i>

285
00:19:45,977 --> 00:19:49,356
<i>Then you must pull</i>
<i>the red lever before you.</i>

286
00:19:49,397 --> 00:19:51,733
<i>But no act comes</i>
<i>without a sacrifice.</i>

287
00:19:51,775 --> 00:19:54,778
- <i>You’ve judged others by</i>
<i>the color of their skin...</i>
- FUCK!

288
00:19:54,819 --> 00:19:57,906
<i>...and today, Evan,</i>
<i>you will learn</i>

289
00:19:57,947 --> 00:20:01,368
<i>that we are all</i>
<i>the same color on the inside.</i>

290
00:20:01,409 --> 00:20:02,911
<i>Live or die, Evan,</i>

291
00:20:02,952 --> 00:20:05,372
<i>the choice is yours.</i>

292
00:20:05,413 --> 00:20:08,833
- <i>( screaming )</i>
- ( engine starts )

293
00:20:08,875 --> 00:20:10,543
NO!

294
00:20:10,585 --> 00:20:14,047
( screaming )

295
00:20:14,089 --> 00:20:17,384
( engine revving )

296
00:20:17,425 --> 00:20:20,470
- Woman: <i>EVAN, HELP!</i>
- I CAN’T.

297
00:20:20,512 --> 00:20:23,723
DO IT.  JUST DO IT.
FUCKING DO IT!

298
00:20:23,765 --> 00:20:25,558
JUST FUCKING DO IT?

299
00:20:25,600 --> 00:20:27,477
DO IT!
DO IT, MAN!

300
00:20:27,519 --> 00:20:29,646
HERE I GO!
( screaming )

301
00:20:34,943 --> 00:20:37,654
EVAN!
BABY, GET ME OUT OF HERE!

302
00:20:37,696 --> 00:20:39,823
SHIT!
FUCK!

303
00:20:39,864 --> 00:20:41,700
HERE I COME!

304
00:20:41,741 --> 00:20:44,703
HERE I COME!
FUCK ME!

305
00:20:49,582 --> 00:20:50,792
HELP ME, PLEASE.

306
00:21:00,802 --> 00:21:03,638
- GOD!
- DO IT!  FUCKING DO IT!

307
00:21:03,680 --> 00:21:06,599
- GOD!
- <i>DO IT!</i>

308
00:21:06,641 --> 00:21:09,394
- EVAN!
- YOU GOT US INTO THIS.

309
00:21:09,436 --> 00:21:11,938
<i>GET US THE FUCK OUT!</i>

310
00:21:11,980 --> 00:21:15,817
- ( screaming )
- <i>DO IT!</i>

311
00:21:18,987 --> 00:21:20,947
YOU’RE A FUCKING PUSSY!

312
00:21:26,453 --> 00:21:28,329
( all screaming )

313
00:21:30,915 --> 00:21:32,834
- ( beeping )
- SHIT.

314
00:22:01,696 --> 00:22:04,491
<i>( woman sobbing )</i>
<i>EVERY NIGHT...</i>

315
00:22:04,532 --> 00:22:08,495
I KEEP THINKING THAT
THINGS WILL GET BETTER

316
00:22:08,536 --> 00:22:10,955
THE NEXT MORNING
WHEN I WAKE UP.

317
00:22:12,207 --> 00:22:14,793
<i>BUT IT ISN’T.</i>

318
00:22:14,834 --> 00:22:18,088
<i>EVERYTHING I DO,</i>

319
00:22:18,129 --> 00:22:19,631
<i>EVERYTHING I SEE,</i>

320
00:22:19,673 --> 00:22:21,758
<i>I’M SURROUNDED</i>
<i>BY THESE</i>

321
00:22:21,800 --> 00:22:24,844
<i>TINY TRIGGERS.</i>

322
00:22:24,886 --> 00:22:26,888
<i>THEY’RE EVERYWHERE,</i>

323
00:22:26,930 --> 00:22:29,099
AND THEY REMIND ME
OF WHAT I WENT THROUGH,

324
00:22:29,140 --> 00:22:33,061
WHAT JIGSAW DID TO ME.
( crying )

325
00:22:33,103 --> 00:22:35,772
SIDNEY, GO ON, PLEASE.

326
00:22:35,814 --> 00:22:39,109
YOU’RE--
YOU’RE IN A SAFE PLACE NOW.

327
00:22:39,150 --> 00:22:42,153
TELL ME
WHAT HAPPENED NEXT.

328
00:22:42,195 --> 00:22:45,740
- ALEX!
STOP, PLEASE!  STOP IT!
- ( grunting )

329
00:22:45,782 --> 00:22:48,743
PLEASE!  ALEX!

330
00:22:52,914 --> 00:22:54,874
- <i>( Alex screams )</i>
- <i>( blades whirring )</i>

331
00:22:54,916 --> 00:22:57,919
( screaming )

332
00:23:01,548 --> 00:23:02,924
SIDNEY, LOOK AT ME.

333
00:23:05,510 --> 00:23:06,970
YOU MADE A DECISION.

334
00:23:07,012 --> 00:23:09,931
<i>HOW DID THAT</i>
<i>MAKE YOU FEEL?</i>

335
00:23:09,973 --> 00:23:12,851
FREE.

336
00:23:12,892 --> 00:23:14,728
HE WAS ABUSIVE.

337
00:23:14,769 --> 00:23:18,690
<i>I TRIED TO STOP IT BEFORE,</i>

338
00:23:18,732 --> 00:23:21,568
BUT IT WASN’T
UNTIL THAT MOMENT

339
00:23:21,609 --> 00:23:22,986
THAT I REALLY DID SOMETHING.

340
00:23:23,028 --> 00:23:26,906
<i>IT WAS HIM OR ME,</i>
<i>AND I CHOSE TO LIVE.</i>

341
00:23:26,948 --> 00:23:28,950
IT WAS THE BEST THING
THAT EVER HAPPENED TO ME.

342
00:23:31,286 --> 00:23:34,831
THAT’S A BUNCH
OF BULLSHIT.

343
00:23:34,873 --> 00:23:37,042
HE HAD TO DIE
FOR YOU TO LEAVE HIM?

344
00:23:40,503 --> 00:23:42,672
YOU WANT TO KNOW WHAT
THE BEST THING THAT
HAPPENED TO ME

345
00:23:42,714 --> 00:23:44,883
AFTER HAVING TO CUT
OFF MY OWN ARM?

346
00:23:48,636 --> 00:23:50,930
IT’S HANDICAPPED PARKING

347
00:23:50,972 --> 00:23:52,724
AT THE DAMN MALL.

348
00:23:56,853 --> 00:24:00,065
WHAT THE HELL IS
A CAMERA HERE FOR ANYWAY?

349
00:24:02,776 --> 00:24:06,196
I AM SIMPLY HERE TO
ILLUSTRATE THE FACT THAT
A TRAUMATIC EXPERIENCE,

350
00:24:06,237 --> 00:24:09,741
SUCH AS THE KIND THAT
EACH ONE OF US HAVE BEEN
FORCED TO ENDURE,

351
00:24:09,783 --> 00:24:12,535
CAN HAVE A POSITIVE
OUTCOME.  THAT’S ALL.

352
00:24:12,577 --> 00:24:15,622
YEAH?
LIKE WHAT?

353
00:24:15,663 --> 00:24:19,000
<i>A NEW PERSPECTIVE ON LIFE.</i>
<i>WHOA WHOA WHOA, WAIT.</i>

354
00:24:19,042 --> 00:24:21,795
I KNOW.

355
00:24:21,836 --> 00:24:25,173
I UNDERSTAND THAT YOU’RE
NOT AT THAT PLACE YET.

356
00:24:25,215 --> 00:24:28,677
<i>I UNDERSTAND THAT</i>
<i>AND I RESPECT THAT.</i>

357
00:24:28,718 --> 00:24:30,178
BUT IF YOU LOOK AROUND
AT ALL THESE PEOPLE

358
00:24:30,220 --> 00:24:32,764
<i>TAKING THEIR LIVES</i>
<i>FOR GRANTED,</i>

359
00:24:32,806 --> 00:24:35,600
<i>EVENTUALLY THEY ALL FOUND</i>
<i>SOMETHING POSITIVE</i>

360
00:24:35,642 --> 00:24:37,936
<i>FROM THEIR EXPERIENCE.</i>

361
00:24:37,977 --> 00:24:40,105
WE SHOULD NEVER BE ASHAMED
OF WHAT WE’VE GONE THROUGH.

362
00:24:40,146 --> 00:24:42,816
BECAUSE WE ARE GOOD
AND WE ARE STRONG!

363
00:24:45,151 --> 00:24:47,153
YOU KNOW WHAT?

364
00:24:47,195 --> 00:24:50,949
I’D LIKE EVERYBODY TO HAVE
A LOOK AT SOMETHING RIGHT HERE.

365
00:24:50,990 --> 00:24:54,869
THESE ARE MY SCARS.

366
00:24:56,871 --> 00:25:00,625
BECAUSE OUR MINDS
WILL HEAL,

367
00:25:00,667 --> 00:25:02,043
BUT THESE SCARS
WILL NEVER GO AWAY.

368
00:25:02,085 --> 00:25:05,839
THESE SCARS SHOULD NOT
BE A SYMBOL OF SHAME.

369
00:25:05,880 --> 00:25:08,049
THEY SHOULD BE WORN
AS A BADGE OF COURAGE.

370
00:25:10,885 --> 00:25:12,137
YOU KNOW, EARLIER,

371
00:25:12,178 --> 00:25:15,306
I SPOKE

372
00:25:15,348 --> 00:25:17,308
OF VALUING
YOUR LOVED ONES.

373
00:25:17,350 --> 00:25:20,020
BUT TO BE PERFECTLY HONEST,

374
00:25:20,061 --> 00:25:23,106
IT’S SOMETHING THAT I NEVER
DID PRIOR TO MY ORDEAL.

375
00:25:23,148 --> 00:25:25,108
BUT SINCE THEN,

376
00:25:25,150 --> 00:25:26,818
I HAVE FOUND SOMEONE

377
00:25:26,860 --> 00:25:29,696
WHO HAS TRULY
BECOME MY ROCK.

378
00:25:32,365 --> 00:25:33,908
JOYCE, IF YOU COULD--

379
00:25:33,950 --> 00:25:36,119
<i>PLEASE.</i>

380
00:25:39,080 --> 00:25:41,291
IT’S MY LOVELY WIFE JOYCE.

381
00:25:42,751 --> 00:25:45,962
- I LOVE YOU.
- I LOVE YOU TOO, BABY.

382
00:25:56,139 --> 00:25:59,351
BRAVO.  HMM.

383
00:25:59,392 --> 00:26:02,687
TO BE ABLE TO SUSTAIN
SUCH A TRAUMATIC EXPERIENCE

384
00:26:02,729 --> 00:26:04,814
<i>AND YET FIND THE POSITIVE</i>

385
00:26:04,856 --> 00:26:07,859
<i>IN THAT GRIZZLY ACT,</i>

386
00:26:07,901 --> 00:26:10,987
IT’S A REMARKABLE FEAT
INDEED.

387
00:26:12,405 --> 00:26:14,407
REMARKABLE,

388
00:26:14,449 --> 00:26:17,827
IF NOT
A LITTLE PERVERSE.

389
00:26:20,121 --> 00:26:23,208
<i>I’M SURE I SPEAK FOR EVERYONE</i>
<i>HERE WHEN I SAY</i>

390
00:26:23,249 --> 00:26:25,835
HOW GRATEFUL WE ARE

391
00:26:25,877 --> 00:26:27,879
TO BE PART OF YOUR

392
00:26:27,921 --> 00:26:31,633
PROMOTIONAL DVD.

393
00:26:39,724 --> 00:26:40,975
I APPRECIATE IT.
THANK YOU.  IT’S--

394
00:26:48,149 --> 00:26:50,694
- I CAN TAKE THAT, SIR.
- THANK YOU VERY MUCH.

395
00:26:50,735 --> 00:26:52,737
JOYCE, CAN I BORROW HIM
FOR A SEC?

396
00:26:52,779 --> 00:26:55,198
- SURE.  I’LL BE
IN THE CAR, OKAY?
- TWO MINUTES BEHIND YOU.

397
00:26:55,240 --> 00:26:56,783
- GREAT.
- YOU’LL SEE HER
TO THE CAR, PLEASE?

398
00:26:56,825 --> 00:26:59,119
- OF COURSE.
- THANK YOU.

399
00:26:59,160 --> 00:27:01,788
WHAT’S UP?

400
00:27:01,830 --> 00:27:03,790
SO WHAT’S WITH
THE CREEPY GUY WITH THE CANE?
SOMEONE I SHOULD KNOW ABOUT?

401
00:27:03,832 --> 00:27:05,208
NO NO NO.
HE’S BEEN AT THESE
MEETINGS LONGER THAN I HAVE.

402
00:27:05,250 --> 00:27:06,960
HE’S FINE.

403
00:27:07,002 --> 00:27:10,005
ALL RIGHT.

404
00:27:10,046 --> 00:27:12,048
LISTEN, GET BACK TO THE HOTEL
AND GET SOME REST, ALL RIGHT?

405
00:27:12,090 --> 00:27:14,134
YEAH.
EVERYTHING’S FINE.

406
00:27:14,175 --> 00:27:15,802
GREAT WORK
TONIGHT, BOBBY.

407
00:27:15,844 --> 00:27:18,013
- THANK YOU.
- YOU’RE THE MAN.

408
00:27:31,359 --> 00:27:33,028
JOYCE?
( gasps )

409
00:27:38,908 --> 00:27:42,203
WHAT HAPPENED TO HIM?

410
00:27:42,245 --> 00:27:44,456
THEY ALWAYS TELL YOU NOT
TO SMOKE AT THE GAS STATION.

411
00:27:44,497 --> 00:27:46,332
THIS SHOULD WRAP UP
THE WEEK FOR YOU.

412
00:27:46,374 --> 00:27:48,335
GREAT.

413
00:27:48,376 --> 00:27:50,879
( cell phone rings )

414
00:27:53,131 --> 00:27:55,008
WHAT’S UP, MAN?

415
00:27:55,050 --> 00:27:58,011
I’M AT A JUNKYARD
ON 58th.

416
00:27:58,053 --> 00:28:00,764
- WHY?
- <i>Call came in</i>
<i>about a car crash.</i>

417
00:28:00,805 --> 00:28:03,058
<i>Car crash?</i>
<i>Why are you there?</i>

418
00:28:03,099 --> 00:28:06,311
IT’S NOT JUST A CAR CRASH.
IT’S A TRAP.

419
00:28:06,353 --> 00:28:08,188
HOW MANY BODIES?

420
00:28:08,229 --> 00:28:10,857
<i>Enough pieces</i>
<i>to make four.</i>

421
00:28:10,899 --> 00:28:13,318
OKAY, GET EVERYONE AWAY
FROM THAT CRIME SCENE
TILL I GET THERE.

422
00:28:13,360 --> 00:28:15,195
- <i>Even Homicide,</i>
<i>you got it?</i>
- YEAH.

423
00:28:15,236 --> 00:28:17,238
ALL RIGHT,
I’M ON THE WAY.

424
00:28:19,074 --> 00:28:20,825
<i>( Jigsaw distorted )</i>
<i>Hello, Evan.</i>

425
00:28:20,867 --> 00:28:22,744
<i>I want to play a game.</i>

426
00:28:22,786 --> 00:28:26,539
<i>The situation</i>
<i>you find yourself in</i>
<i>is of your own doing.</i>

427
00:28:26,581 --> 00:28:29,292
<i>You, your girlfriend</i>
<i>and your friends</i>

428
00:28:29,334 --> 00:28:31,503
<i>are all racists.</i>

429
00:28:31,544 --> 00:28:34,130
<i>You have intimidated others</i>

430
00:28:34,172 --> 00:28:37,342
<i>based on their</i>
<i>physical differences...</i>

431
00:28:37,384 --> 00:28:39,761
<i>( distortion )</i>

432
00:28:49,104 --> 00:28:51,106
- <i>( police radio chatter )</i>
- <i>( sirens wailing )</i>

433
00:28:53,358 --> 00:28:55,443
SO WHAT DO YOU THINK?

434
00:28:57,112 --> 00:28:59,155
WHY?

435
00:28:59,197 --> 00:29:01,366
WHY THIS DISPLAY?

436
00:29:01,408 --> 00:29:03,535
WHY THEM?
WHY NOW?

437
00:29:03,576 --> 00:29:06,246
YOU KNOW HE LIKES
TO PUT ON A SHOW.

438
00:29:06,287 --> 00:29:09,874
WELL, IT’S GOTTA
BE SOMETHING ELSE.

439
00:29:17,090 --> 00:29:20,176
BAG THE OTHER BODIES.
GET THEM BACK TO THE CORONER’S
OFFICE RIGHT AWAY.

440
00:29:20,218 --> 00:29:22,303
WE’LL NEED THEM CHECKED
FOR ANYTHING RESEMBLING
A CLUE--

441
00:29:22,345 --> 00:29:25,473
<i>TATTOOS, PIERCINGS,</i>
<i>SKIN CUTTINGS.</i>

442
00:29:25,515 --> 00:29:28,560
IF THAT MAN HAS A CAVITY
IN HIS TOOTH, I WANT TO
KNOW ABOUT IT.

443
00:29:28,601 --> 00:29:30,270
- YES SIR.
- ALL RIGHT.

444
00:29:30,311 --> 00:29:33,314
- GIBSON.
- YEAH?

445
00:29:33,356 --> 00:29:36,609
HOFFMAN WAS EXPECTING YOU.

446
00:29:36,651 --> 00:29:38,445
Man:
<i>PUT ON YOUR GLOVES.</i>

447
00:29:38,486 --> 00:29:39,863
( sniffs )
GOD DAMN.

448
00:29:43,241 --> 00:29:46,953
WOULD YOU LOOK AT THAT?
PLEASE GET FORENSICS IN HERE.

449
00:29:46,995 --> 00:29:49,414
<i>TELL THEM TO HAUL ASS.</i>

450
00:29:49,456 --> 00:29:52,459
THIS NEEDS TO BE DUSTED
FOR PRINTS.

451
00:29:52,500 --> 00:29:55,128
- ALL RIGHT.
- OKAY.

452
00:30:11,269 --> 00:30:13,521
( grunts )

453
00:30:23,156 --> 00:30:24,032
( groans )

454
00:30:28,078 --> 00:30:30,205
HELP!

455
00:30:40,507 --> 00:30:42,384
( static hisses )

456
00:30:47,263 --> 00:30:50,308
Hello, Bobby.

457
00:30:50,350 --> 00:30:51,893
I want
to play a game.

458
00:30:51,935 --> 00:30:54,396
<i>You have amassed wealth,</i>

459
00:30:54,437 --> 00:30:56,564
<i>fame and notoriety</i>

460
00:30:56,606 --> 00:30:59,442
based upon your story
of survival.

461
00:30:59,484 --> 00:31:01,528
<i>Many have aided</i>
<i>in your cause,</i>

462
00:31:01,569 --> 00:31:04,364
<i>but few know the truth.</i>

463
00:31:04,406 --> 00:31:06,533
You are a liar.

464
00:31:06,574 --> 00:31:09,119
You and I both know you have
never been in a trap,

465
00:31:09,160 --> 00:31:12,664
nor have
you ever been tested.

466
00:31:12,706 --> 00:31:16,292
<i>Today these lies</i>
<i>will come full circle</i>

467
00:31:16,334 --> 00:31:17,711
<i>and you will learn</i>

468
00:31:17,752 --> 00:31:20,422
if you truly have
what it takes

469
00:31:20,463 --> 00:31:23,717
to call yourself
a survivor.

470
00:31:23,758 --> 00:31:25,552
The cage you find
yourself in

471
00:31:25,593 --> 00:31:28,263
<i>will symbolize</i>
<i>your rebirth.</i>

472
00:31:29,514 --> 00:31:33,226
JOYCE?
NO!

473
00:31:33,268 --> 00:31:36,146
JOYCE!  NO!

474
00:31:36,187 --> 00:31:38,148
<i>PLEASE, NO.</i>

475
00:31:38,189 --> 00:31:40,066
Within the next
60 minutes,

476
00:31:40,108 --> 00:31:43,194
<i>you must stay</i>
<i>upon the path of learning</i>

477
00:31:43,236 --> 00:31:45,655
and traverse a series
of obstacles

478
00:31:45,697 --> 00:31:48,074
to obtain access
to your wife,

479
00:31:48,116 --> 00:31:50,243
who you also have deceived.

480
00:31:50,285 --> 00:31:53,163
If you fail to reach her
before the clock runs out,

481
00:31:53,204 --> 00:31:55,123
- <i>she will die.</i>
- NO.

482
00:31:55,165 --> 00:31:57,959
Live or die, Bobby?
Make your choice.

483
00:32:07,802 --> 00:32:11,264
<i>( mechanical whirring )</i>

484
00:32:11,306 --> 00:32:13,725
( screams )

485
00:32:34,371 --> 00:32:36,039
( grunting )

486
00:33:11,574 --> 00:33:13,493
BOBBY!

487
00:33:13,535 --> 00:33:16,663
HELP!

488
00:33:16,705 --> 00:33:19,165
HELP!

489
00:33:19,207 --> 00:33:21,751
LET ME OUT!

490
00:33:30,385 --> 00:33:33,763
BOBBY.  BOBBY!

491
00:33:33,805 --> 00:33:37,726
WHAT’S GOING ON?
WHAT’S GOING ON?

492
00:33:37,767 --> 00:33:40,437
TV Announcer:
<i>Another Jigsaw survivor</i>
<i>has come forward.</i>

493
00:33:40,478 --> 00:33:44,357
<i>As the city stays</i>
<i>crippled in fear from</i>
<i>the Jigsaw killings,</i>

494
00:33:44,399 --> 00:33:47,652
chilling new words from
the latest survivor
provide a reminder

495
00:33:47,694 --> 00:33:49,446
<i>of the physical</i>
<i>and mental toll</i>

496
00:33:49,487 --> 00:33:52,073
<i>these deadly games</i>
<i>can take.</i>

497
00:33:52,115 --> 00:33:54,367
This horrible event

498
00:33:54,409 --> 00:33:56,411
was happening to me,

499
00:33:56,453 --> 00:33:59,497
and in that moment,

500
00:33:59,539 --> 00:34:03,126
<i>that moment that</i>
<i>this thing</i>

501
00:34:03,168 --> 00:34:05,545
<i>threatened</i>
<i>to take everything away,</i>

502
00:34:05,587 --> 00:34:07,464
even the pain...

503
00:34:09,883 --> 00:34:13,261
I realized what
I still had left to give.

504
00:34:13,303 --> 00:34:15,847
<i>And I didn’t want</i>
<i>to let that go.</i>

505
00:34:17,599 --> 00:34:21,311
It gave me light.

506
00:34:21,353 --> 00:34:23,480
That pure moment

507
00:34:23,521 --> 00:34:26,232
<i>of absolute horror</i>
<i>gave me light.</i>

508
00:34:26,274 --> 00:34:29,319
And as wrong
as this may seem,

509
00:34:29,361 --> 00:34:32,447
I’m better
for enduring it.

510
00:34:32,489 --> 00:34:35,200
I’m stronger.

511
00:34:35,241 --> 00:34:38,578
<i>And I must admit,</i>
<i>I’m grateful for it.</i>

512
00:34:38,620 --> 00:34:41,790
I’m grateful
it happened to me.

513
00:34:41,831 --> 00:34:44,751
And I wish the same
for everyone like me.

514
00:34:44,793 --> 00:34:47,170
Announcer:
<i>Joan is but one of a growing</i>
<i>number of citizens...</i>

515
00:34:47,212 --> 00:34:49,422
IF SOMETHING LIKE
THAT DOESN’T GET YOU

516
00:34:49,464 --> 00:34:52,425
TO CHANGE
YOUR PERSPECTIVE ON LIFE,

517
00:34:52,467 --> 00:34:54,719
I DON’T KNOW WHAT WILL.

518
00:34:54,761 --> 00:34:56,721
YEAH.

519
00:34:56,763 --> 00:34:59,307
( scoffs )

520
00:34:59,349 --> 00:35:00,934
AND IF THOSE PEOPLE WEREN’T
SO FUCKED UP AFTER THEIR GAMES,

521
00:35:00,975 --> 00:35:03,436
THEY’D MAKE A MINT
SELLING THEIR STORIES.

522
00:35:44,811 --> 00:35:47,230
OH SHIT.

523
00:35:50,734 --> 00:35:52,652
SHIT.

524
00:36:09,294 --> 00:36:12,672
WELL, THAT’S A REAL
CLEVER DESIGN.

525
00:36:12,714 --> 00:36:16,468
YOURS OR YOUR HUSBAND’S?

526
00:36:16,509 --> 00:36:19,512
- EVERYTHING WAS HIM.
- RIGHT.  WELL, HERE’S
MY PROBLEM.

527
00:36:19,554 --> 00:36:20,847
THAT WAS LEFT FOR ME

528
00:36:20,889 --> 00:36:24,267
AND YOUR FINGERPRINTS
WERE ALL OVER IT.

529
00:36:24,309 --> 00:36:26,478
WHEN YOU TOLD ME HOFFMAN
HAD IT IN FOR YOU,

530
00:36:26,519 --> 00:36:28,730
YOU DIDN’T MENTION THAT
IT WAS BECAUSE YOU TRIED
TO KILL HIM.

531
00:36:30,899 --> 00:36:33,693
THERE’S A NEW
GAME GOING ON.

532
00:36:33,735 --> 00:36:35,612
DOES THAT SURPRISE YOU?

533
00:36:35,653 --> 00:36:37,280
NO.

534
00:36:37,322 --> 00:36:40,367
NO?  NO?

535
00:36:40,408 --> 00:36:43,411
YOU’RE CRAZY,
YOU KNOW THAT?

536
00:36:43,453 --> 00:36:45,872
<i>I KNEW YOU WERE CRAZY</i>
<i>THE MINUTE I LAID</i>
<i>EYES ON YOU.</i>

537
00:36:45,914 --> 00:36:48,500
CRAZY.

538
00:36:48,541 --> 00:36:52,671
OKAY, THIS IS
WHAT WE’RE GONNA DO,
CRAZY.

539
00:36:52,712 --> 00:36:54,673
TILL I CATCH
MARK HOFFMAN,

540
00:36:54,714 --> 00:36:57,884
THIS IS YOUR NEW HOME.
GET COMFY.

541
00:36:57,926 --> 00:37:00,428
WHAT MAKES YOU THINK
HE CAN’T FIND ME HERE?

542
00:37:00,470 --> 00:37:04,265
JILL, IT’S A SAFE HOUSE.
SAFE HOUSE.

543
00:37:04,307 --> 00:37:06,768
SAFE HOUSE.
YOU GET IT?

544
00:37:10,563 --> 00:37:13,525
GIBSON,
THIS WAS SENT HERE

545
00:37:13,566 --> 00:37:15,819
ADDRESSED TO JILL.
HOFFMAN KNOWS
OUR LOCATION.

546
00:37:15,860 --> 00:37:18,446
GOD DAMN IT.
GOD DAMN IT!

547
00:37:18,488 --> 00:37:20,448
- ( cell phone rings )
- WHAT?

548
00:37:20,490 --> 00:37:23,743
WE JUST HAD
A SMALL EXPLOSION HERE
IN A CAR AT THE CRIME SCENE.

549
00:37:23,785 --> 00:37:25,745
- <i>Okay,</i>
<i>is anyone hurt?</i>
- OH SHIT!

550
00:37:35,422 --> 00:37:38,591
- ROGERS?
ROGERS, YOU OKAY?
- YEAH.

551
00:37:38,633 --> 00:37:40,677
GET OUT OF THERE.
YOU GET THE BOMB SQUAD
TO SWEEP THE YARD.

552
00:37:40,719 --> 00:37:44,097
<i>Don’t touch anything else</i>
<i>until it’s clean.</i>

553
00:37:44,139 --> 00:37:45,682
- GOT IT.
- <i>All right.</i>

554
00:37:45,724 --> 00:37:47,642
PLAY IT.

555
00:37:53,481 --> 00:37:55,483
Hello, Gibson.

556
00:37:55,525 --> 00:37:58,319
<i>Been a long time.</i>

557
00:37:58,361 --> 00:38:01,364
What I want is simple.
Give me Jill Tuck.

558
00:38:01,406 --> 00:38:03,450
<i>You’re protecting her</i>
<i>despite the fact</i>

559
00:38:03,491 --> 00:38:05,452
<i>that she had direct</i>
<i>knowledge throughout,</i>

560
00:38:05,493 --> 00:38:09,456
which makes her complicit
in every death.

561
00:38:09,497 --> 00:38:11,791
<i>I’ll make you a deal.</i>

562
00:38:11,833 --> 00:38:14,461
Give her to me.

563
00:38:14,502 --> 00:38:16,379
The game stops
and no one else dies.

564
00:38:16,421 --> 00:38:18,882
<i>If not,</i>

565
00:38:18,923 --> 00:38:21,051
everyone dies
and you’ll be to blame.

566
00:38:21,092 --> 00:38:24,054
<i>Make your choice.</i>

567
00:38:24,095 --> 00:38:26,348
The clock’s ticking.

568
00:38:28,475 --> 00:38:30,894
LET’S GET HER DOWN
TO THE HOLDING CELL
AT THE STATION.

569
00:38:30,935 --> 00:38:33,563
LOCK IT DOWN.
NO ONE GETS IN
WITHOUT MY AUTHORITY.

570
00:38:33,605 --> 00:38:35,523
GOT IT.

571
00:38:51,623 --> 00:38:54,042
<i>( woman whimpering )</i>
<i>OH MY GOD.</i>

572
00:38:55,627 --> 00:38:58,546
OH GOD!  NO!  PLEASE!
( screaming )

573
00:39:00,215 --> 00:39:02,634
NO!  PLEASE!

574
00:39:02,676 --> 00:39:05,887
PLEASE, NO!
GOD DAMN IT!

575
00:39:05,929 --> 00:39:08,848
BOBBY.
BOBBY, HELP ME!

576
00:39:08,890 --> 00:39:11,726
YOU’VE GOT TO GET
ME OUT OF HERE.

577
00:39:11,768 --> 00:39:13,853
I CAN’T MOVE, BOBBY.

578
00:39:13,895 --> 00:39:17,023
- PLEASE, HELP ME!
- OKAY OKAY OKAY.
JUST RELAX.

579
00:39:18,817 --> 00:39:20,944
OW.

580
00:39:20,985 --> 00:39:23,613
OW!

581
00:39:23,655 --> 00:39:26,116
<i>HELP ME!</i>
<i>DO SOMETHING!</i>

582
00:39:26,157 --> 00:39:27,909
DON’T LEAVE ME.

583
00:39:30,537 --> 00:39:32,038
Jigsaw:
<i>Hello, Bobby.</i>

584
00:39:32,080 --> 00:39:34,916
<i>Before you is one</i>
<i>of your trusted colleagues.</i>

585
00:39:34,958 --> 00:39:37,752
<i>She has been your</i>
<i>publicist for years,</i>

586
00:39:37,794 --> 00:39:39,713
<i>knowing your lies,</i>

587
00:39:39,754 --> 00:39:42,590
<i>but choosing</i>
<i>to speak no evil.</i>

588
00:39:42,632 --> 00:39:45,719
<i>She has been</i>
<i>richly rewarded</i>
<i>for her words,</i>

589
00:39:45,760 --> 00:39:49,723
<i>but today she will be</i>
<i>rewarded for her silence.</i>

590
00:39:49,764 --> 00:39:52,434
<i>In the X-ray,</i>
<i>you will see a key,</i>

591
00:39:52,475 --> 00:39:55,228
<i>the key</i>
<i>to Nina’s survival,</i>

592
00:39:55,270 --> 00:39:57,480
<i>which will shut off</i>
<i>her device.</i>

593
00:39:57,522 --> 00:39:59,482
<i>But there’s a catch.</i>

594
00:39:59,524 --> 00:40:02,235
<i>You have one minute</i>
<i>to pull the fish hook</i>
<i>from her stomach</i>

595
00:40:02,277 --> 00:40:04,529
<i>and unlock her device</i>

596
00:40:04,571 --> 00:40:08,158
<i>or else the four spikes</i>
<i>will penetrate her throat,</i>

597
00:40:08,199 --> 00:40:10,952
- <i>silencing Nina forever.</i>
- FUCK!

598
00:40:10,994 --> 00:40:13,538
<i>Remember, the spikes</i>
<i>will also advance</i>

599
00:40:13,580 --> 00:40:16,624
<i>each time the decibel level</i>
<i>in this room</i>

600
00:40:16,666 --> 00:40:18,501
<i>rises above a whisper,</i>

601
00:40:18,543 --> 00:40:20,462
<i>killing her even sooner.</i>

602
00:40:20,503 --> 00:40:23,757
- <i>Will Nina live</i>
<i>or die, Bobby?</i>
- ( screaming )

603
00:40:23,798 --> 00:40:26,259
<i>The choice is yours.</i>

604
00:40:26,301 --> 00:40:28,678
HELP ME.
HELP!

605
00:40:28,720 --> 00:40:30,680
- NO!
- ( muffled screaming )

606
00:40:30,722 --> 00:40:33,099
<i>( ticking )</i>

607
00:40:33,141 --> 00:40:34,851
JUST SHUT UP.

608
00:40:34,893 --> 00:40:37,896
STAY WITH ME, OKAY?

609
00:40:43,318 --> 00:40:48,031
DO IT.
( grunting )

610
00:40:48,073 --> 00:40:49,741
( screaming )

611
00:40:51,826 --> 00:40:54,788
NO. NO. NO.

612
00:40:54,829 --> 00:40:57,957
OKAY, STAY WITH ME.
STAY WITH ME.

613
00:40:57,999 --> 00:41:00,960
IT’S GONNA BE OKAY.
LOOK AT ME.
LOOK AT ME.

614
00:41:01,002 --> 00:41:02,128
( whimpers )

615
00:41:08,301 --> 00:41:10,095
( screams )

616
00:41:13,264 --> 00:41:15,975
NO!  NINA, QUIET.

617
00:41:16,017 --> 00:41:19,604
PLEASE PLEASE, FOR ME.
JUST SHUT THE FUCK UP.

618
00:41:19,646 --> 00:41:21,606
I’M GONNA GET THIS OUT.

619
00:41:21,648 --> 00:41:22,857
( ticking )

620
00:41:27,904 --> 00:41:29,864
( gagging )

621
00:41:35,662 --> 00:41:37,080
- ( screams )
- NO!  NO!

622
00:41:37,122 --> 00:41:39,708
JUST DO IT, BOBBY.

623
00:41:39,749 --> 00:41:40,875
JUST FUCKING DO IT.

624
00:41:45,046 --> 00:41:46,756
( coughs )

625
00:41:54,264 --> 00:41:55,974
( screaming )

626
00:42:02,397 --> 00:42:03,982
( screaming )

627
00:42:08,695 --> 00:42:09,612
BOBBY!

628
00:42:27,714 --> 00:42:28,882
NO!

629
00:42:31,176 --> 00:42:33,720
WHY WOULDN’T YOU JUST
SHUT THE FUCK UP?!

630
00:42:35,680 --> 00:42:37,682
YOU JUST NEEDED
TO SHUT UP!

631
00:42:40,935 --> 00:42:44,856
Joyce:
<i>NO!  OH MY GOD!</i>

632
00:42:44,898 --> 00:42:48,151
NO!  HELP!

633
00:42:48,193 --> 00:42:51,613
( shrieks )

634
00:42:51,654 --> 00:42:54,074
HELP!  HELP!

635
00:43:26,690 --> 00:43:29,734
HERE YOU ARE, MA’AM.
TAKE CARE.

636
00:43:29,776 --> 00:43:31,361
MA’AM, YOUR NAME?

637
00:43:31,403 --> 00:43:34,656
SARA-- WITHOUT AN H.

638
00:43:35,949 --> 00:43:38,952
I JUST WANT TO SAY
I LOVE YOUR BOOK SO MUCH.

639
00:43:38,993 --> 00:43:42,122
I JUST FELT LIKE I COULD
FEEL EVERYTHING THAT
YOU WENT THROUGH.

640
00:43:42,163 --> 00:43:44,749
I FEEL LIKE IT
CHANGED MY LIFE.

641
00:43:44,791 --> 00:43:46,001
I APPRECIATE THAT, MA’AM.

642
00:43:47,460 --> 00:43:49,879
I REALLY DO.
THANK YOU.

643
00:43:49,921 --> 00:43:52,841
THANK YOU.

644
00:44:00,056 --> 00:44:01,349
<i>YOUR NAME, SIR?</i>

645
00:44:01,391 --> 00:44:03,101
JOHN.

646
00:44:03,143 --> 00:44:05,311
WITH AN H,

647
00:44:05,353 --> 00:44:07,355
WITHOUT AN H,
IT DOESN’T MATTER.

648
00:44:07,397 --> 00:44:10,150
WE’LL GO WITH JOHN
WITH AN H THIS TIME.

649
00:44:10,191 --> 00:44:12,318
YOU GOT QUITE
AN ARMY WORKING
FOR YOU HERE, DON’T YOU?

650
00:44:12,360 --> 00:44:15,780
MUST BE SPREADING
A PRETTY GOOD WORD.

651
00:44:15,822 --> 00:44:18,783
WELL, WE TRY TO REACH AS MANY
PEOPLE AS POSSIBLE, YOU KNOW?

652
00:44:18,825 --> 00:44:20,827
YOU DON’T SEE ANYTHING
WRONG WITH THAT?

653
00:44:20,869 --> 00:44:23,913
( laughs ) NO.
NO SIR, I DON’T.

654
00:44:27,876 --> 00:44:29,711
YOU KNOW,

655
00:44:29,753 --> 00:44:32,130
HISTORY IS A PASSION
FOR ME.

656
00:44:32,172 --> 00:44:34,716
<i>AND IN ANCIENT EGYPT</i>
<i>IF YOU WERE SPEAKING</i>
<i>UNDER OATH,</i>

657
00:44:34,758 --> 00:44:36,301
<i>YOU WERE REQUIRED TO SAY,</i>

658
00:44:36,343 --> 00:44:38,803
"IF I’M LYING,

659
00:44:38,845 --> 00:44:41,306
TAKE ME TO THE QUARRIES."

660
00:44:43,850 --> 00:44:45,935
THAT MEAN
ANYTHING TO YOU?

661
00:44:45,977 --> 00:44:48,355
NO SIR.
NO SIR, IT DOESN’T.

662
00:44:48,396 --> 00:44:50,440
WELL, I’LL TELL YOU
WHAT IT MEANS.

663
00:44:50,482 --> 00:44:53,318
IT MEANS
IF YOU KNOWINGLY LIED

664
00:44:53,360 --> 00:44:56,196
ON THE PUBLIC RECORD

665
00:44:56,237 --> 00:44:57,906
THAT YOU WERE SUBJECT
TO A PERIOD OF ENSLAVEMENT.

666
00:44:57,947 --> 00:44:59,824
WHAT ARE YOU
IMPLYING HERE, SIR?

667
00:44:59,866 --> 00:45:01,493
I’M NOT IMPLYING ANYTHING.

668
00:45:01,534 --> 00:45:04,996
MOVE ALONG, BUDDY.
HE SIGNED YOUR BOOK.

669
00:45:05,038 --> 00:45:08,375
THANKS FOR THE SIGNATURE.

670
00:45:08,416 --> 00:45:12,337
NICE PICTURE,
BUT I DON’T NEED IT.

671
00:45:12,379 --> 00:45:13,922
WE’VE MET.

672
00:45:26,893 --> 00:45:29,062
ADAM, GIBSON SAYS HE WANTS
YOU ON THESE RIGHT AWAY.

673
00:45:29,104 --> 00:45:31,147
